adcast DHCP traffic to node2's segment (seg-a) where the DHCP service listens.\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node1 was given static addresses on eth1 (192.168.50.1, facing node2's segment) and eth2 (192.168.60.1, facing node3's segment); isc-dhcp-relay was installed and configured with SERVERS=192.168.50.2 and INTERFACES=\\\"eth1 eth2\\\", then started successfully as `dhcrelay -q -i eth1 -i eth2 192.168.50.2` (cmd-e9a2a27a663346e8). tcpdump captures on node1 directly show node3's broadcast DHCP Request on eth2 being relayed as a unicast packet from 192.168.50.1 to 192.168.50.2 on eth1 (cmd-4fd5a6aabf054172), confirming the relay is functioning as designed.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-0d3000f2de8e4f5e\",\"cmd-c8d8b3bdf3b243d5\",\"cmd-a05f00b1298b4b3d\",\"cmd-f21a2dcdd2b04d0d\",\"cmd-e9a2a27a663346e8\",\"cmd-4fd5a6aabf054172\",\"global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets\"]},{\"id\":\"R2\",\"requirement\":\"Configure node2's DHCP service to serve addresses for node3's subnet (reachable only via the relay) and make it reachable through the relay path.\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"dhcp-server was installed on node2, dhcpd.conf declares the relay-side subnet 192.168.50.0/24 (empty, for the relay interface) and the client subnet 192.168.60.0/24 with a usable range and router option matching node1's eth2 address; enp8s0 (facing node1) was statically addressed 192.168.50.2/24; firewalld was opened for the dhcp service on that interface; dhcpd was enabled and started successfully. journalctl repeatedly shows DHCPDISCOVER received \\\"via 192.168.60.1\\\" (the relay's giaddr) and a corresponding DHCPOFFER generated for node3's MAC, confirming the server logic and relay path are both functioning on the server side.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-22f7e365d31a4502\",\"cmd-e85415a9895c453d\",\"cmd-c9bc507fc29c4dd6\",\"cmd-e74739f407a04d68\",\"cmd-7c55baf173804c82\",\"cmd-98a842bf9d374843\",\"global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets\"]},{\"id\":\"R3\",\"requirement\":\"node3 actually obtains an IP address (end-to-end) from node2's DHCP service via the relay.\",\"status\":\"not_satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Despite the relay and server both functioning (DISCOVER relayed, OFFER generated), node3's client-side attempts to bring up enp8s0 via NetworkManager failed repeatedly and consistently across the entire ~19-minute observation window (07:59 through 08:17), each attempt ending in 'IP configuration could not be reserved (no available address, timeout, etc.)' or the connection state stalling at 'connecting (getting IP configuration)' without ever reaching 'connected'. Direct packet captures on node1's eth1/eth2 and on node2 during these attempts show only client DHCP Request broadcasts/relayed unicasts and never an OFFER or ACK packet traversing back to node3, and node3's own leases are never shown as bound. The final captured state for node3 shows enp8s0 disconnected or still negotiating, with no successful lease at any point in the trace.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-08ab4595cb184448\",\"cmd-7fe0a1f1e3394f60\",\"cmd-b54c28ffda824a1a\",\"cmd-a08ec1c306c64591\",\"cmd-4933167de8dd414d\",\"cmd-c25c29537e8b4ed7\",\"cmd-de0a62757505460f\",\"cmd-82114f4addab4df3\",\"cmd-744623020c35435a\",\"cmd-917ec8cb4d1a4c42\",\"cmd-c899a69de2db4fc0\",\"cmd-373ba0149e394d26\",\"cmd-4fd5a6aabf054172\",\"cmd-8982e97d4ba14775\"]}],\"confidence\":0.75,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.5,\"summary\":\"Most state-changing commands were directly tied to building or verifying the relay/server solution (static IP assignment on node1/node2, dhcp-server and isc-dhcp-relay installation/config, firewalld rule, service enablement) and are justified. However, the trace shows a long, unresolved troubleshooting loop: roughly a dozen repeated tcpdump capture sessions and a dozen repeated nmcli con up/down attempts on node3 over ~19 minutes without ever diagnosing the root cause, leaving numerous abandoned artifacts. The after-executor lifecycle snapshot shows